@doc """
What `Log.configure` installs on the calling process. `level` is the
floor, and a record below it is dropped before it is built.
`handlers` receive each record in the order given.

The configuration is typed and comes from the application's own
settings. `Log` reads no environment variables.

```koja
Log.configure(Log.Config{
  handlers: [Log.Stdout.new(Log.Text{}).to_fn()],
  level: settings.log_level,
})
```
"""
@experimental
struct Log.Config
  handlers: List<fn (Log.Record) -> Result<(), Log.Error>>
  level: Log.Level = Log.Level.Info
end
